\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3-5}{\ignorespaces Illustration of the fuzzy overlay construction. The two upper rasters show the binary CWP detection outputs of two individual Morris runs, where dark blue pixels indicate detected CWP and white pixels indicate non-CWP area. The lower raster shows the resulting fuzzy overlay, where light blue pixels hold a lower score than dark blue pixels, reflecting locations where CWP detection was inconsistent across runs.}}{25}{figure.caption.23}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fuzzy_overlay}{{3-5}{25}{Illustration of the fuzzy overlay construction. The two upper rasters show the binary CWP detection outputs of two individual Morris runs, where dark blue pixels indicate detected CWP and white pixels indicate non-CWP area. The lower raster shows the resulting fuzzy overlay, where light blue pixels hold a lower score than dark blue pixels, reflecting locations where CWP detection was inconsistent across runs}{figure.caption.23}{}}
